{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_636240a2f69e93500e7e4b8ac2d65f1f31b0d95b4afa7fd55c0737bdabf90a55"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the test suite runs with pytest and --doctest-modules, and integration tests create real git repositories and worktrees, session-scoped to avoid repeated node-init overhead."}],"claim_ids":["clm_636240a2f69e93500e7e4b8ac2d65f1f31b0d95b4afa7fd55c0737bdabf90a55"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:11Z","created_by_operation":"op_f8909e523a7743ddb94dd5b5fdd7d3b9","id":"pg_3ee90b2567f45678bfae25872e00a157","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/plasma-ai-fractal-agents-md-18793200c0d7-25872e00a157.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b3ac798603eb52eb84536fdc15ef8485"],"title":"plasma-ai/fractal/AGENTS.md @ 18793200c0d7","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:11Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f8909e523a7743ddb94dd5b5fdd7d3b9"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_05af5b814a1cbf5c2e845cc41e492577d47cae6367f9d8b4ff8c798e534f746a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The package installs from PyPI as plasma-fractal (or via the fractal pointer dist); pipx/uv tool installs additionally require installing plasma-wiki, which a plain pip install pulls automatically."},{"claim_ids":["clm_17fd4c65296c6d73ffa4e5be34e760b87a1e82383e0fc43bf5346128bf0e8e0c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The fractal CLI exposes commands such as 'fractal open' to launch the dashboard from a project root (requires an initialized fractal), with a --light flag for light terminal color schemes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_38064d19540729b12ea6de440cab3b14ab349a21c6cab3023d586669bb17a657"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Nodes run their agents without permission prompts by default: seeded configs disable approval gates (e.g. Claude bypassPermissions, Codex danger-full-access), and the per-node worktree isolates only the branch, not the filesystem or network."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ec9812806f4f85adeb4fe3c3f68d995c04650e714826ddaaa4ec1107eec2921"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /fractal skill takes a plain-language directive, distills NODE.md instructions and a parameter table, asks for anything it could not infer, and launches the node in a tmux session once approved."},{"claim_ids":["clm_636240a2f69e93500e7e4b8ac2d65f1f31b0d95b4afa7fd55c0737bdabf90a55"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the test suite runs with pytest and --doctest-modules, and integration tests create real git repositories and worktrees, session-scoped to avoid repeated node-init overhead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_67119f3542a0adba768ff8a080c6c85d931708962c7b17ba3befcde6bc9afece"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: pull requests should branch from and target 'dev' rather than 'main', which advances only at releases; setup uses install.sh or uv sync with pre-commit hooks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7353749749fe72459707aca87dcf12fcf1bb6fd4852ceb9398ad26fc5fe2b76f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each loop is bounded by hard caps on iterations, depth, children, cost, and time, and an operator can steer or stop it at any point."},{"claim_ids":["clm_aac1b603c26d0a704e01a646184d33f08e271fdab997e7b1ea52410684c2a583"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All state — runs, iterations, steps, costs, and signals — is tracked in a local SQLite database that can be interacted with live in a terminal UI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ca8d630fc8b0ba34f6e1291385fabc70f4b6bd1706ab8de0fb0a8a679efef197"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent loops arrange into a tree of git worktrees: a node iterates toward a goal and spawns child nodes for separable subtasks, so the tree grows to fit the problem rather than following a fixed plan."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d37ffad7aee44c8cc1ccf58e09bc7ab4d59413fea5ed4948e551f8dee681a5e2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The fractal skill can be installed via plugin marketplace for Claude Code and Codex, or via 'fractal install', which copies or symlinks skills into ~/.claude/skills and ~/.agents/skills."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fbda7301173f5d07e230dd79c0f3eec4e0177d2bf7b5d88132926368e900fd47"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Five agent backends are supported — Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build, OpenCode, and Oh My Pi — selected per node with --agent, with OpenRouter routing available via --provider=openrouter or native model ids."}],"claim_ids":["clm_05af5b814a1cbf5c2e845cc41e492577d47cae6367f9d8b4ff8c798e534f746a","clm_17fd4c65296c6d73ffa4e5be34e760b87a1e82383e0fc43bf5346128bf0e8e0c","clm_38064d19540729b12ea6de440cab3b14ab349a21c6cab3023d586669bb17a657","clm_3ec9812806f4f85adeb4fe3c3f68d995c04650e714826ddaaa4ec1107eec2921","clm_636240a2f69e93500e7e4b8ac2d65f1f31b0d95b4afa7fd55c0737bdabf90a55","clm_67119f3542a0adba768ff8a080c6c85d931708962c7b17ba3befcde6bc9afece","clm_7353749749fe72459707aca87dcf12fcf1bb6fd4852ceb9398ad26fc5fe2b76f","clm_aac1b603c26d0a704e